  <section class="sec prose col">
    <div class="num"><span class="num__n">2</span><h2>More caffeine is still the same answer</h2></div>
    <p>Switch from coffee to an energy drink and the packaging changes.</p>
    <p>The afternoon strategy does not.</p>
    <p>You are still turning the same volume knob higher and hoping this time the result feels different.</p>
    <p>That is why the familiar alternatives do not feel like much of an escape:</p>
    <div class="card card--paper">
      <ul class="rows">
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="6" ry="9" transform="rotate(-30 12 12)"/><path d="M8 17c3-3 5-6 8-10" transform="rotate(-30 12 12)"/></svg></i>Coffee with a different roast</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="7" y="4" width="10" height="17" rx="2"/><path d="M9 4V2h6v2"/><path d="M10 9h4M10 13h4"/></svg></i>An energy drink in a louder can</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 19C5 9 11 5 20 4c0 9-4 15-14 15z"/><path d="M5 19c3-4 6-7 10-9"/><path d="M14 14l3 3"/></svg></i>A “natural energy” product with caffeine hiding behind green packaging</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 8h12v6a5 5 0 0 1-5 5H9a5 5 0 0 1-5-5z"/><path d="M16 10h2a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-2"/><path d="M19 3l2 2-2 2"/></svg></i>Another cup because the last cup stopped carrying you</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <img src="{{ 'lpi-escalation-lineup.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1024" height="570" alt="Overhead view of a desk with an empty mug, a takeaway coffee cup, an unbranded green energy drink can, and a glass of water in a row">
      <figcaption>Different container. Same basic conversation with your nervous system.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>At some point, the better question is not, “How much more can I add?”</p>
    <p class="big">It is, “What else is there?”</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec prose col">
    <div class="num"><span class="num__n">3</span><h2>The answer is a different plant, not caffeine wearing a leaf costume</h2></div>
    <p>That is where Kratom enters the picture.</p>
    <p>Kratom comes from <em>Mitragyna speciosa</em>, a Southeast Asian tree in the coffee family.</p>
    <figure>
      <img src="{{ 'lpi-kratom-leaves-macro.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1024" height="768" alt="Close-up of glossy green kratom leaves with red veins and water droplets against a dark background">
      <figcaption><em>Mitragyna speciosa.</em> Same family as coffee. Not the same plant.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>But Kratom is not coffee with a new label. It is not another caffeine blend wearing green packaging. It is a different plant with a different kind of experience.</p>
    <p>At lower amounts, Kratom leans toward energy and focus. At higher amounts, it leans toward body ease and relaxation.</p>
    <div class="range" aria-label="How the amount changes the experience">
      <div class="range__bar"><span class="range__dot"></span></div>
      <div class="range__ends">
        <span><b>Lower amounts</b>Energy and focus</span>
        <span><b>Higher amounts</b>Body ease<br class="m"> and relaxation</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>That dose-dependent range is the part most newcomers miss.</p>
    <div class="aside">
      <img src="{{ 'lpi-dandy2-rocky-flex.webp' | asset_url }}" width="560" height="560" alt="Illustration of the Dandy raccoon flexing both arms">
      <p>You are not trying to blast yourself with more stimulation. You are looking for the amount that fits the moment.</p>
    </div>
    <p>And if the moment is the afternoon slump, a small starting point makes more sense than immediately reaching for the strongest option on the shelf.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec prose col">
    <div class="num"><span class="num__n">4</span><h2>A berry gummy makes the first try much easier</h2></div>
    <p>Kratom has a reputation for being complicated.</p>
    <p>Powder. Scoops. Bitter taste. Guesswork.</p>
    <p>That is not a great way to introduce a new plant to somebody who is already standing in the kitchen negotiating with a half-empty coffee pot.</p>
    <p>Dandy Mixed Berry Gummies give you a simpler entry point.</p>
    <figure>
